import json,pathlib
H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_pfp_infrastructure_remaining';p=H/(P+'_notes.json');n=json.loads(p.read_text())
rows={
488:('SPJA contract explicitly includes bag join multiplicity, nonnull AVG count and before/after group keys, delegating event repair to BQNF.','m*delta is sufficient only when matching multiplicity remains fixed or before/after contributions are both available; simultaneous join changes need cross terms. Median can have finite full-carrier state even though no fixed-size additive statistics suffice; unsupported is implementation scope.'),
489:('ASRF improves the deprecated hash-only alias by requiring authenticated distinct producer/evaluator roles and declared acyclic evaluation graph, explicitly denying incompleteness/cohomology claims.','Distinct principals can collude and graph completeness is external. Hash inequality of actor and artifact is not independence; no authentication implementation provided and verifier_required false.'),
490:('Lightcone contract separates consensus serialization, interval order and physical propagation and gives conservative interval bounds.','Inside a speed cone establishes causal possibility, not actual influence/message receipt; speed maximum alone does not guarantee network path delivery. Negative time difference can be past-timelike rather than spacelike despite named ruled_out_spacelike rule. Requires positive speed and valid bounds.'),
491:('Clock contract uses initial offset plus elapsed-time drift bound, explicit epochs and abstention for overlap, correctly distinguishing unknown order from budget exhaustion.','Requires certified finite nonnegative rates/elapsed times, common frame and trustworthy reset log. Bounded measurements do not prove future drift stays inside declaration; disjointness gives order only within those premises.'),
492:('Cyclic form correctly takes least rotation, distinguishes periodic necklaces from Lyndon words, excludes empty input and separates canonicalization from original phase.','An orbit reconstructs only up to rotation; original position needs retained offset. Linear-time Booth/Duval claim concerns an available algorithm, not an implementation/test in this YAML; no physical meaning or universal subshift supplied.'),
493:('Representation GNF correctly separates exact protected semantics, degraded ledger outcome and byte integrity, and explicitly denies physical-gauge interpretation.','Semantic correspondence and commutation witnesses must actually be evaluated under specified schema meaning; generic declarations do not decide semantics. Failure terminal Reject is outside its local terminal list, requiring canonical/local vocabulary handling.'),
494:('Token form states fixed38-symbol lexical carrier, unique decoding and re-encoding identity, with no semantic or authorization claim.','One returned tokenization does not prove uniqueness among alternatives. Alphabet filtering alone cannot establish structured-value bijection; erasure must reject forbidden bytes rather than silently trim them. Actual decoder and inverse remain unspecified.'),
495:('Trace form correctly requires symmetric irreflexive independence, accepted-step diamond at reached prefixes and guard reads as well as writes. It explicitly limits replay to endpoint equivalence and retains history for original interleaving.','No local evaluator supplied. All allowed swaps need semantic commutation evidence, not just disjoint writes; finite trace instances do not establish all-program independence.'),
496:('ZFNF gives correct reduced rational representation and primal Ax>=b,x>=0 / dual A^Ty<=c,y>=0 convention with recomputed objectives, feasibility and exact zero gap.','Rational bit growth/resources and parser canonicality remain implementation matters. Polyhedral inequalities and bilinear gap are not a cochain complex merely because residual spaces are named; positive gap shows the pair is not jointly optimal.'),
497:('Security EFNF correctly requires independently sound permission projection before typed temporal commutation and keeps host authorization separate; failure is discrepancy, not automatic leak.','Permission soundness remains explicitly open; Boolean witness and hashes do not establish noninterference or authenticate principal. Decidability requires finite admitted policy language and transition population, not arbitrary policy code.'),
498:('GTMUR requires descent compatibility, loss accounting, update commutation and target verifier acceptance.','certification.verifier_required and loss_ledger_required are false despite mandatory criteria, risking metadata-driven bypass. Chi declaration is not actual natural transformation/commuting witness; earlier actual adapter false-positive findingF009 is independent execution evidence.'),
499:('WDNF requires finite support with distinct witness pair and irreflexive relation, explicitly not infinite separation or execution authority.','Irreflexivity alone does not make complement an equivalence relation; quotient reconstruction requires symmetry/cotransitivity or separately supplied equivalence. Carrier size>=2 is necessary for a nontrivial distinct pair but not sufficient evidence of an asserted relation.'),
500:('Complete ten-entry typed domain index read: all marked extended form and not true relational NF, with explicit null authority effect.','Index is a selected catalog, not exhaustive enforcement; short names EFNF/LCNF elsewhere collide, so canonical identity must drive lookup. No source evaluation or proof in this table.'),
502:('Packaged-demo receipt contract explicitly distinguishes fixture replay, live integrity-only custody, typed refusal reproduction and illustration from proof, using canonical bounded JSON and full source/artifact bindings.','Contract describes intended runtime obligations; previously reviewed execution owner and controls expose admission gaps. No new replay/live call here; hashes show consistency not authorship, as stated.'),
}
